{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Avenge the vengeance of the children of Israel</b> — this is juxtaposed to the parashah of vows to teach you that vows are made in a time of distress and war. And further they said: one who is silent toward his daughter and his wife and does not annul [their vows] — he is taken in their place. The Midianites who caused Israel to sin — all the more so shall they be punished." "<b>Afterward you shall be gathered</b> — because he saw the deed of Midian and did not act zealously for the Name, therefore he was held obligated for the vengeance of Midian." "<b>El amekha</b> — plene yod, to teach you that in ten (יו״ד) places his death is mentioned in the Torah."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:28.334245029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}